# Superseded capture: a whole-room scan taken in Scaniverse's Area mode while the
# subject was still the plush. Nothing references it and it is 21MB. Kept on disk as a
# record, but not worth carrying in history — delete this line to start tracking it.
assets/plush/

# Downloaded benchmark ground truths (see assets/benchmark/SOURCES.md)
assets/benchmark/*
!assets/benchmark/SOURCES.md

# Benchmark and completion outputs. Mostly regenerable, but completion/out also holds
# the chess-photos run, which is not: back it up before deleting.
completion/out/

# Local Python environment for completion/ tools (never commit)
.venv/
# Local AI model checkouts + weights for the B3 spike (multi-GB, never commit)
.models/

__pycache__/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Test recorder runs (serve.py writes them; see docs/testing/README.md). Raw runs and
# FLAGS.md are machine-local: they hold this browser/machine's details and churn on every
# run. Timmy curates what matters into the committed docs/testing/LEDGER.md instead.
docs/testing/runs/

# Local crash-safe backups of uncommitted work (Stop hook, .claude/hooks/backup.sh)
.backups/

# Agent worktrees (Claude Code isolation)
.claude/worktrees/
